{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's intricate rhythms and heavy sound; Train Of Thought also appeals through that combination.",
    "Master of Puppets and Cowboys from Hell connect with the aggressive riffs I enjoy in In Flames and 3 Inches of Blood, while Fallen fits the melodic, accessible side of my rock listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Kid A does not fit what I want now because electronic experimentation does not give me the guitar-driven heaviness drawing me to the other choices.",
    "Sgt. Pepper's psychedelic pop feels distant from my current interest in heavy riffs and darker rock, even though it belongs to the broader world of rock music."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in rock seems to have been stretched too broadly, as though it also meant I wanted experimental electronic sounds or psychedelic pop right now.",
    "Several Metallica albums fit my broad taste, but treating them as equally compelling misses why I would choose Master of Puppets before St. Anger or Metallica today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent listening to 10.000 Days makes intricate, heavy music especially appealing now, beyond a general interest in hard rock.",
    "I respond to both aggressive riffs and melodic heaviness, but a plausible match alone does not mean I would choose it now; Ride the Lightning appeals, yet Master of Puppets takes priority."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices mostly understand my interest in heavy and melodic rock, but some stretch that interest too broadly and miss my current pull toward intricate rhythms and aggressive guitar riffs."
}"}
